        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued November 19 at 12:54PM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "At 1253 PM PST, Doppler radar was tracking gusty showers capable of\nproducing a landspout near Camp Pendleton South, or 7 miles southwest\nof Camp Pendleton, moving northeast at 25 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Possible waterspout north of Oceanside may move ashore\nand wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible. Gusty winds\ncould knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured\nobjects.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nCamp Pendleton and Camp Pendleton North.",
